#Brayis-prep.lic
#Warrior version of Fizzleworth-prep.lic (Brayis) -- no spellcasting, no
#instrument, no wands, so gearing up for combat is clearing hands, rubbing the
#couple of items he can use without a spellcasting skill, and readying the
#weapon.
#
#Katana, not the Claidhmore, for now -- "ready weapon"/"store weapon", not the
#"2weap" noun (that's specific to the two-handed Claidhmore). "grip two" after
#readying makes sure it's actually being wielded two-handed instead of GS4's
#one-handed default grip for it.

module BrayisPrep

# clear hands -- "store weapon" routes the katana to the readied sheath per
# the in-game STORE config (STORE SET WEAPON SHEATH); "stow all" mops up
# anything left in the off-hand.
fput "store weapon"
fput "stow all"

# rub stuff, but only if the spell isn't already active -- and only pause
# after ones that actually ran, instead of always eating 3s per item
unless Spell[1712].active?
  Script.run("qverb", "rub small statue")
  pause 3
end
unless Spell[509].active?
  Script.run("qverb", "rub white crystal")
  pause 3
end

fput "ready weapon"

# Still nothing in either hand: the weapon is really gone (disarmed and never
# recovered, or the STORE weapon setting points at something that isn't
# there). Don't let bigshot walk back out unarmed -- Brayis died on 10/22 doing
# exactly that after a death dirge disarmed him. Stop bigshot here, in town,
# where it's safe, the same way unlost.lic stops it when it's stuck. This runs
# before any travel (bigshot's hunting_prep_commands happen at the start of
# pre_hunt). Skips `grip two` too, which just prints its usage with no weapon.
pause 0.5
if checkright.nil? && checkleft.nil?
  echo "Brayis-prep: nothing in hand after READY WEAPON -- stopping bigshot. " \
       "Check the STORE weapon setting (STORE LIST) and this script's ready/grip commands."
  Script.kill("bigshot") if Script.running?("bigshot")
  exit
end

fput "grip two"

# Puts away loot eloot has no room for and unpauses it, so a full cloak can't
# leave you fighting with your hands full (see eloot_guard.lic).
Script.start("eloot_guard") unless Script.running?("eloot_guard")

end #End of module
